        "prompt": "$x=\\dfrac{t-1}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1\\le t\\le5$",
          "worked": "The highlighted section has $0\\le x\\le2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}0&\\le\\frac{t-1}{2}\\le2\\\\0&\\le t-1\\le4\\\\1&\\le t\\le5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p69-q63-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x=2\\cos t$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}+2k\\pi\\le t\\le\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}+2k\\pi$, $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n\nFor example, $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\le t\\le\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ covers the highlighted section.",
          "worked": "The highlighted section has $0\\le x\\le2$, so\n$$\\begin{align*}0&\\le2\\cos t\\le2\\\\0&\\le\\cos t\\le1\\end{align*}$$\nOn the interval $-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le t\\le\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, test the endpoints and an intermediate value:\n$$\\begin{align*}x\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)&=0\\\\x(0)&=2\\\\x\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus this interval covers the entire highlighted section. Since cosine has period $2\\pi$, all admissible values are\n$$-\\frac{\\pi}{2}+2k\\pi\\le t\\le\\frac{\\pi}{2}+2k\\pi,\\qquad k\\in\\mathbb Z.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p69-q63-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=t-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1\\le t\\le2$",
          "worked": "The highlighted section has $0\\le y\\le1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}0&\\le t-1\\le1\\\\1&\\le t\\le2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
